    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "It's more than just a pattern, though. The specific way they're handling the supply chain bottlenecks reminds me so much of the exact errors I saw the Imperial Cabinet make during the mobilization phases. Back then, we underestimated how quickly a single point of failure could paralyze the entire northern front. If someone with my specific background in those old-world strategic maneuvers were to look at the current blockade through that lens, what specific vulnerabilities should I be looking out for in the modern naval logistics?",
